Subject: [PATCH] meson: link D-Bus independently of PipeWire features

kde_night_light.c is always compiled and uses libdbus directly. Keep D-Bus in
the base dependency list so builds with both PipeWire features disabled work.

Rebased onto 6.0.1: the 5.15.2 hunk failed only on an adjacent context line,
because the C++-to-C rewrite changed the add_project_arguments language from
['c', 'cpp'] to 'c'. The structure is otherwise unchanged -- src/kde_night_light.c
is still in the unconditional source list and still includes dbus/dbus.h, and
dbus-1 is still declared only inside the pipewire block.
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@
     dependency('libdrm'),
     dependency('wayland-egl'),
     dependency('wayland-client'),
+    dependency('dbus-1'),
 ]
 
 if build_machine.system() == 'linux'
@@ -137,7 +138,6 @@
     dep += [
         dependency('libpipewire-0.3'),
         dependency('libspa-0.2'),
-        dependency('dbus-1'),
     ]
     add_project_arguments('-DGSR_DBUS', language : 'c')
 endif
